---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Relevance from '../components/Relevance.astro';
import { DATASET_USE, REVIEW_STATUS } from '../lib/vocab';
import { loadCatalog } from '../lib/catalog';
const catalog = await loadCatalog();
const counts = {
  datasets: catalog.datasets.length,
  methods: catalog.methods.length,
};
---

<Base title="About & Editorial Policy" description="What Pathology Atlas is, how entries are verified, and what each relation label means.">
  <article class="wrap pt-12">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl md:text-5xl">A resource atlas, edited like a reference work</h1>
    <div class="prose-atlas mt-6 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Pathology Atlas helps computational pathology researchers find usable data, reproducible methods and the papers behind
        them, starting from an organ, a disease or a task. It is deliberately small: {counts.datasets} datasets and
        {counts.methods} methods in this release, each checked against primary sources.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is a static site. There is no account, no tracking, no hosted slide viewer and no mirrored data. Links go to the
        official portals.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section id="editorial-policy" aria-labelledby="policy-h" class="rule-t mt-12 pt-6">
      <h2 id="policy-h" class="text-3xl">Editorial policy</h2>

      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="prose-atlas">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl">Sources come first</h3>
          <p>
            Awesome lists and aggregators are used only to discover candidates. Facts are checked against the original paper, the
            project or challenge site, the official repository, the model card or the data portal. Each scale figure, access route,
            licence and dataset relation names the source it came from.
          </p>
          <h3 class="mb-2 mt-6 text-xl">Original writing</h3>
          <p>
            Summaries are written by the editors. We do not paste abstracts or README text, and we do not reproduce figures or
            pathology images whose licence is unclear. Illustrations on this site are original, abstract drawings.
          </p>
          <h3 class="mb-2 mt-6 text-xl">Unknown means unknown</h3>
          <p>
            A field we have not confirmed reads <span class="not-verified">Not verified</span>. We do not estimate counts, infer
            licences or fill gaps from memory. <code class="font-mono text-sm">last_verified</code> is only set on the date an
            editor actually checked the sources.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl">Review status</h3>
          <dl class="mt-3 divide-y divide-rule border-y border-rule text-sm">
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr]">
              <dt class="font-semibold">{REVIEW_STATUS.verified}</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink-2">Sources checked; shown on the public site and in list search.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr]">
              <dt class="font-semibold">{REVIEW_STATUS['needs-review']}</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink-2">Drafted from primary sources, awaiting a second check. Kept in the repository only.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr]">
              <dt class="font-semibold">{REVIEW_STATUS.draft}</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink-2">Candidate found during discovery. Kept in the repository only.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl">What a relation means</h3>
          <dl class="mt-3 space-y-4 text-sm">
            <div>
              <dt><Relevance kind="benchmark" size="md" /></dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink-2">
                A cited source reports the method with this dataset for this task. The recorded use is one of:
                {Object.values(DATASET_USE).join(', ').toLowerCase()}.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Relevance kind="same-task" size="md" /></dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink-2">
                The method targets the same task family (for example weakly supervised slide classification). No result on the
                dataset is recorded. This is a pointer, not evidence of performance.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Relevance kind="background" size="md" /></dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink-2">Reading that explains the task or its labels, such as a grading consensus paper.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-atlas mt-10">
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl">Corrections and new entries</h3>
        <p>
          Entries live as YAML and Markdown files in the repository and are validated at build time for duplicate IDs, invalid
          values, broken links between entries and facts without a source. New entries start as draft and only become public after
          review. See the repository README for the workflow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
